<HEAD><style>/* Readable Detail — page sheet. The typeset technical handbook: hairline rules group,
   weight and column position make hierarchy, one accent means "read this first".
   Every colour routes through theme vars; classes carry shape and rhythm only. */

.gml-card {
  --rule: var(--divider-color);
  --hairline: 0.75pt;
  /* A figure caption clears the image crop by a full line of air (renderer knob). */
  --caption-hug-gap: 15pt;
}

/* ── Signature move 3: the topic rule. Every seam in the deck is ONE hairline in the
   theme's divider colour. Grids wearing these register classes draw designed seams. ── */
.sidehead, .columns, .toc, .faq, .steps, .checks, .roles, .pillars, .cover-meta, .stats, .compare {
  --grid-divider-color: var(--rule);
  --grid-divider-width: var(--hairline);
}
.rule.gml-divider { --divider-color: var(--rule); --divider-thickness: var(--hairline); border-radius: 0; }

/* ── Signature move 8: the short accent tick — cover, closing, dark act breaks only. ── */
.tick.gml-divider { --divider-color: var(--accent-color); --divider-thickness: 2pt; border-radius: 0; }
.tick.gml-divider .gml-divider__rule { width: 40pt; margin-inline-start: 0; border-radius: 0; }

/* ── Signature move 1: the side-head. Label column beside a reading column, a hairline
   above each group; the text clears the seam by the seam inset. ── */
.sidehead { --grid-seam-inset: 14pt; }
.sidehead .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 8pt; }

/* ── Signature move 2: the lede — one 17pt opening sentence, held to a reading measure. ── */
.lede.gml-paragraph { max-width: 600pt; }

/* ── Signature move 4: the running index — "02 · Receiving and release", one per body card. ── */
.meta.gml-paragraph { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin-block-end: calc(var(--block-gap) * 0.6); }

/* ── Signature move 5: the figure caption — "Figure 4 — a full sentence." (lead in bold serif) ── */
.gloss.gml-paragraph { max-width: 560pt; margin-block-start: calc(var(--block-gap) * 0.5); }

/* ── Signature move 6: the ledger table — plate-tinted sans header row, hairline row rules,
   no vertical rules, numbers right-aligned in tabular figures. ── */
.ledger {
  --table-border-width: var(--hairline);
  --table-border-color: var(--rule);
  --table-header-bg: var(--surface-color);
  --table-header-color: var(--body-color-muted);
  --table-header-weight: 600;
  --table-header-font: var(--heading-font);
  --table-cell-padding: 8pt 12pt 8pt 8pt;
  --table-radius: 0;
}
.ledger .gml-table__cell { font-size: calc(13 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); }
.ledger .gml-table__row[data-header] .gml-table__cell { font-size: calc(11 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
.ledger .gml-table__cell.num { text-align: end; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.ledger .gml-table__row:last-child .gml-table__cell { border-bottom: var(--table-border-width) solid var(--table-border-color); }

/* ── Signature move 7: the claim row — a small caps label beside one sentence. ── */
.claim .gml-label-group { --label-pad-inline: 0; --label-pad-block: 0; }
.claim .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 4pt; }

/* Cover meta ledger: label/value cells separated by hairline seams (cover-meta class). */
.cover-meta { --grid-seam-inset: 16pt; }
.cover-meta .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 4pt; }

/* Stat figures: tabular numerals on display nodes. */
.metric { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.stats { --grid-seam-inset: 16pt; --cell-decor-color: var(--accent-color); }
.stats .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 6pt; }

/* Reading columns (two- and three-column text): a tighter paragraph beat inside a column
   than between groups, and a hairline seam between columns. */
.columns { --grid-seam-inset: 22pt; }
.prose .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 10pt; }

/* Marker numerals and glyphs (agenda, procedure, checklist) set in the heading sans, tabular. */
.toc .gml-grid-cell__marker, .steps .gml-grid-cell__marker, .checks .gml-grid-cell__marker { font-family: var(--heading-font); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

/* Agenda contents ledger: muted numerals in a fixed gutter. */
.toc { --marker-color: var(--body-color-muted); --marker-inline-size: 36pt; --marker-gap: 14pt; --grid-seam-inset: 14pt; }

/* Numbered procedure: accent numerals inline-left, editorial rows on hairline seams. */
.steps { --marker-color: var(--accent-color); --marker-font-size: 22pt; --marker-font-weight: 700; --marker-inline-size: 44pt; --marker-gap: 16pt; --grid-seam-inset: 14pt; }
.steps .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 8pt; }

/* Checklist: accent check marks (symbol markers) in the gutter, generous row air. */
.checks { --marker-color: var(--accent-color); --marker-font-weight: 700; --marker-inline-size: 22pt; --marker-gap: 12pt; --grid-seam-inset: 16pt; }

/* FAQ ledger: question column beside answer column, hairline above each pair. */
.faq { --grid-seam-inset: 14pt; }
.faq .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 6pt; }

/* Icon-led registers: ink glyphs sized to their text, hairline seams. */
.roles { --marker-color: var(--heading-color); --marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 14pt; --grid-seam-inset: 14pt; }
.pillars { --marker-color: var(--heading-color); --grid-seam-inset: 18pt; }
.pillars .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 8pt; }

/* Comparison columns: peer cells on hairline seams, a tighter beat inside each. */
.compare { --grid-seam-inset: 18pt; }
.compare .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 8pt; }

/* Figure plates: square corners and a hairline keyline around in-flow figures. */
.plate .gml-figure__img { border: var(--hairline) solid var(--rule); border-radius: 0; }
.plate.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 0; }

/* Evidence cells (chart + gloss) keep the caption close to the plot. */
.evidence .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 8pt; }

/* Pull quote: a 2pt accent bar, the one accent moment on that card. */
.quote.gml-blockquote { padding-inline-start: 22pt; }
.quote.gml-blockquote > .gml-blockquote__bar { width: 2pt; border-radius: 0; background: var(--accent-color); }

/* Dark act breaks and the closing (root cell painted ink): rules and ticks lift to the
   lightened accent so they read on the ground. */
.act { --rule: var(--body-color-muted); }
.act .tick.gml-divider { --divider-color: var(--palette-3); }
.act .gml-grid-cell__content { --block-gap: 14pt; }

/* Statement: one display-scale claim held to a measure. */
.statement .gml-title { max-width: 760pt; }

/* Running footer: the page number in the sans, tabular. */
.gml-card__footer { font-family: var(--heading-font); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: var(--body-color-muted); }</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="N_FjIW3D2B" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pT2NeTHaE-" colspan="36"><display size="md">Project Meridian:<br>handover pack for the incoming owner</display><p font-size="lg" class="lede">The facts, decisions, operating rhythm and unresolved work you need to take over Kestrel Data’s billing replacement.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xxs" class="tick"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="hug" class="cover-meta"><grid-item id="gJdEbfWziv" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="plain">AUTHOR</label></labels><p font-size="sm">Priya Raghunathan, outgoing owner</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZAmGF4dGF2" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="plain">PACK WRITTEN</label></labels><p font-size="sm">23 September 2026</p></grid-item><grid-item id="W7b_nzYOkZ" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="plain">FOR</label></labels><p font-size="sm">Incoming project owner</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="FW64lya_ST" class="plate" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/fGAZaONKHFuw6pAeuOGRu.jpg" saved-media-id="1psyll5a65mjm1r" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="figure" alt="Documentary photograph of a finance systems specialist standing at a billing operations wall, checking payment and invoice exception patterns with a small project team working behind her, natural daylight, three-quarter view, one focal subject, real depth, naturalistic colour, no legible text or logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:2560,&quot;has_transparency&quot;:false}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="a3FLOyKawq"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="48su7andIu"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">00 · Before you read</p><h1>This is a fictional worked example</h1><p font-size="lg" class="lede">Kestrel Data, Project Meridian, and every name, figure, contract and date in this pack are invented to demonstrate what a complete handover looks like. Nothing here describes a real company or real results.</p><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="fill" class="columns"><grid-item id="u8OIfDu0CU" class="prose" colspan="30"><h3>The fictional setting</h3><p><b>Kestrel Data</b> is a B2B workforce analytics company with 310 staff and 1,180 customers.</p><p><b>Project Meridian</b> replaces its homegrown billing system with the vendor platform Nomad Billing.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1VfoX1IYqU" class="prose" colspan="30"><h3>How to read the figures</h3><p>The pack was written on <b>23 September 2026</b> by Priya Raghunathan, the outgoing owner.</p><p>Figures marked <i>assumption</i> are illustrative planning inputs, not measurements. Everything else is presented as the project’s own recorded numbers.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="bR0yvvTQKf"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="joDUlScXw1"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">00 · Executive summary</p><h1>Where Meridian stands today, in one page</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="sidehead"><grid-item id="TomESPyPMC" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="3Kb6WumG71" colspan="14"><h4>Overall</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="HZJS5wU2ii" colspan="40"><p font-size="sm"><b>Amber.</b> Delivery is on track; budget and one dependency are not.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="bXHDabwDWK" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="MPKqwj9JBQ" colspan="14"><h4>Phase 1</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="lYXKm_FOqK" colspan="40"><p font-size="sm">Catalog, invoicing and payments have been live since <b>4 May 2026</b>. All new business has used Nomad since that date.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="ZZwY55H4b5" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ls_n9Ptbrg" colspan="14"><h4>Phase 2</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="fMBaeJU6h6" colspan="40"><p font-size="sm"><b>707 of 1,140</b> eligible accounts have moved, 62% complete. Eight waves remain, ending 14 January 2027.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="apajD_igS6" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="cMrb2mAgH-" colspan="14"><h4>Phase 3</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="u22BjFrspX" colspan="40"><p font-size="sm">Revenue recognition and dunning have not started. The target is <b>26 February 2027</b>.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="mFGFwROGZJ" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="cRmVJOnSit" colspan="14"><h4>Budget</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="_-xvdoPPNU" colspan="40"><p font-size="sm">$2.40M approved, $1.52M spent and a $2.61M forecast. The forecast is an assumption and is <b>8.75% over</b>; approval is pending.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="GWoQbiX8z7" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="U3hiMDJU7f" colspan="14"><h4>Biggest risk</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="d1PdWXqMbG" colspan="40"><p font-size="sm"><b>88 complex accounts</b> have no proven migration pattern.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="unG2CbRIxp"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="_JhRTEeX4a"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">00 · Contents</p><h1>How this pack runs</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="toc"><grid-item id="yiBsW872co" vertical-align="center"><h4>Context and scope</h4><p>Why Meridian exists, what it covers and what it deliberately leaves elsewhere.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ejXO_fF-ra" vertical-align="center"><h4>Where things stand</h4><p>Status by workstream, migration numbers, budget and invoice quality.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="s8_B7s8PnW" vertical-align="center"><h4>How it runs</h4><p>Cadence, systems, access, the incident runbook and the vendor relationship.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="GQSsAso_mB" vertical-align="center"><h4>People and decisions</h4><p>Owners, settled decisions, open calls, risks and external dependencies.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="rzVae0vx4-" vertical-align="center"><h4>Your first ninety days</h4><p>Sequenced actions, unanswered questions and the terms of this handover.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="naf6gLgdAS" vertical-align="center" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none" class="act"><grid-item id="_IoKoajmzX" background-color="palette-2"><display size="xl" class="metric"><span text-color="palette-3">01</span></display><hr color="palette-3" thickness="md" width="xxs" class="tick"><h1>Context and scope</h1><p font-size="lg">Why Kestrel replaced BillingSvc, what Meridian is responsible for, and the boundaries you should defend when new requests arrive.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="MuuBO29nQC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="T7AFk1vmbl"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">01 · Context and scope</p><h1>Billing was the constraint on every pricing decision Kestrel wanted to make</h1><p font-size="lg" class="lede">BillingSvc was written in 2017 for one annual seat-based plan sold in USD.</p><grid divider="0.75pt" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="sidehead"><grid-item id="ty_TpM5tdf" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="ycGQ8K1hq5" colspan="15"><h4>Pricing stayed frozen</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="iRnQyWqCOI" colspan="39"><p font-size="sm">Usage-based and hybrid plans needed engineering work per contract. Sales maintained <b>41 bespoke arrangements</b> by hand.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="Us-CS45CFq" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="g6OaMAT7AN" colspan="15"><h4>Close took too long</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="2rDjTfZ5qx" colspan="39"><p font-size="sm">Finance spent <b>9 of 10 close days</b> reconciling invoices in spreadsheets.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="btnEkHvD-J" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="9DiCIILXi0" colspan="15"><h4>Customers saw errors</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="4vc4g0XNlD" colspan="39"><p font-size="sm"><b>4.8%</b> of invoices needed a manual correction in June 2026.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="rLrtnmms5T" padding="9pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="gnVJaazhvJ" colspan="15"><h4>Ownership was absent</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="OrQ3lwHdtV" colspan="39"><p font-size="sm">Two part-time engineers, no roadmap and no test coverage on proration.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The board approved Meridian in December 2025 on an assumed three-year payback built from the 2025 cost base. It is not a measured result.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="TUeSvlYH34"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Hxg2jpW52P"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">01 · Context and scope</p><h1>What Meridian covers</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="fill" class="columns"><grid-item id="CNItWtkV4b" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>Subscription catalog</h4><p font-size="sm">Plans, add-ons, ramps and discounts become configurable without a deploy.</p><h4>Invoicing and payments</h4><p font-size="sm">Generation, delivery, card and ACH collection, and credit notes.</p><h4>Tax</h4><p font-size="sm">Calculation and filing data through Tessera Tax across <b>34 jurisdictions</b>.</p><h4>Dunning</h4><p font-size="sm">Automated retry and escalation for failed payments in Phase 3.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="_EJtectkup" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>Revenue recognition</h4><p font-size="sm">ASC 606 schedules generated from contract terms in Phase 3.</p><h4>Self-serve checkout</h4><p font-size="sm">The public purchase flow, re-pointed to Nomad.</p><h4>Account migration</h4><p font-size="sm">Move <b>1,140 eligible accounts</b> and their <b>4,190 subscriptions</b> off BillingSvc. Kestrel has 1,180 customers; 40 perpetual-licence accounts are carved out, so every migration figure uses 1,140 as its denominator.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="x3hUD3mpOc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="K01G2HM70r"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">01 · Context and scope</p><h1>What Meridian deliberately does not cover</h1><p font-size="lg" class="lede">Each exclusion was a steering-committee decision, not an oversight. Resist requests to absorb them.</p><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="fill" class="columns"><grid-item id="DXnkBUiG_W" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>Usage metering pipeline</h4><p font-size="sm">Data Platform owns it. Meridian consumes the API and does not rebuild it.</p><h4>Sales-assisted quoting UI</h4><p font-size="sm">It stays in Salesforce CPQ under Deal Desk.</p><h4>Multi-entity consolidation</h4><p font-size="sm">Deferred to FY28 with the EMEA entity work.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="0NNFiJsnd0" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>Payment and commission extensions</h4><p font-size="sm">No wallets, crypto or regional rails beyond SEPA. Commission calculation remains in the Sales Ops spreadsheet model.</p><h4>Legacy perpetual licences</h4><p font-size="sm"><b>40 accounts</b> run off in BillingSvc through FY28 and are never migrated. Subtracting them from 1,180 customers gives the 1,140 eligible base.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-ysExYSOCJ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="TwDA0FhQTJ"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">01 · Context and scope</p><h1>Three phases, one cutover per wave, sixteen waves in total</h1><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Jan–Mar 2026 · Phase 0</h4><p>Vendor selection, contract and data-model mapping. Complete.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Apr–May 2026 · Phase 1</h4><p>Catalog, invoicing and payments live for new business on 4 May. Complete.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Jun 2026–Jan 2027 · Phase 2</h4><p>Sixteen fortnightly Thursday waves. Eight complete; eight remain. In flight.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Nov 2026–Feb 2027 · Phase 3</h4><p>Revenue recognition and dunning. Target 26 February. Not started.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>FY28 · Phase 4</h4><p>BillingSvc decommission. Not funded; date undecided.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><hr class="rule"><p role="caption">Waves 1–8 ran 4 and 18 June; 2, 16 and 30 July; 13 and 27 August; and 10 September. Waves 9–16 run 8 and 22 October; 5 and 19 November; 3, 17 and 31 December; and 14 January. No wave ran on 24 September while the complex-account design was pending.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="knU6z5Qcmn" vertical-align="center" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none" class="act"><grid-item id="8gzxELo681" background-color="palette-2"><display size="xl" class="metric"><span text-color="palette-3">02</span></display><hr color="palette-3" thickness="md" width="xxs" class="tick"><h1>Where things stand</h1><p font-size="lg">Delivery is moving, but the remaining migrations are harder, the budget decision is late and invoice accuracy has stopped improving.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="iXjf0ZmNXi"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Q6n19O2YiY"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">02 · Where things stand</p><h1>Status by workstream</h1><table col-widths="[23,12,47,18]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="ledger"><tbody><tr><td><p>Workstream</p></td><td><p>Status</p></td><td><p>Current position</p></td><td><p>Owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Migration waves</b></p></td><td><p>Green</p></td><td><p>707 of 1,140 eligible accounts live. Wave 9 ships 8 October.</p></td><td><p>Hannah Blum</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Complex accounts</b></p></td><td background-color="palette-1"><p>Red</p></td><td><p>88 accounts with multi-year ramps or custom terms have no migration pattern. Design due 23 October.</p></td><td><p>Marcus Oyelaran</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Tax integration</b></p></td><td><p>Amber</p></td><td><p>Live in 34 jurisdictions; 19 EU rounding discrepancies remain in the exception ledger.</p></td><td><p>Tomás Iriarte</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Revenue recognition</b></p></td><td><p>Amber</p></td><td><p>Design signed off. Build has not started and depends on an open decision.</p></td><td><p>Tomás Iriarte</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Self-serve checkout</b></p></td><td><p>Green</p></td><td><p>Live since 4 May. Any redesign waits for Growth’s pricing test.</p></td><td><p>Project owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Legacy run-off</b></p></td><td><p>Green</p></td><td><p>BillingSvc frozen and read-only for migrated accounts; two engineers remain on call.</p></td><td><p>Engineering</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Fj968C0Lw9"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="a3aYJGTN2K"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">02 · Where things stand</p><h1>Migration is 62% done and the remainder is the hard part</h1><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="IkKa6YcCDI" class="evidence" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><graph chart-type="donut" show-data-labels="true" color-scheme="theme" width="470pt" height="275pt"><properties><property key="status" label="Account status" type="label"></property><property key="accounts" label="Eligible accounts" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>Migrated</cell><cell>707</cell></row><row><cell>Remaining</cell><cell>433</cell></row></data></graph><p role="caption" class="gloss"><b>Figure 1 —</b> 707 migrated and 433 remaining from the 1,140 eligible-account base.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="pZPB9CgeGy" class="prose" colspan="25"><display size="md" class="metric">88</display><p><b>remaining accounts are complex.</b> No migration pattern exists for them yet.</p><p>Eight completed waves averaged 88 accounts. Eight remaining waves average about 54 and end 14 January 2027.</p><p>The eligible base carries 4,190 active subscriptions; migrated accounts carry 2,612.</p><p role="caption">Two completed waves slipped by one week. None was rolled back, and no customer-visible billing outage has been traced to a wave.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="S-On_X5XJc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pAQ4hc7b8K"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">02 · Where things stand</p><h1>Budget is forecast 8.75% over, driven by one scope change</h1><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="hug" class="stats"><grid-item id="oAThbijdpO" border="lg solid" border-sides="top" colspan="20"><display size="md" class="metric">$2.40M</display><p font-size="sm" class="gloss">Approved: $1.05M vendor, $0.98M internal delivery and $0.37M contingency.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="HzXGfltUjt" border="lg solid" border-sides="top" colspan="20"><display size="md" class="metric">$1.52M</display><p font-size="sm" class="gloss">Spent to 31 August, 63% of the approved budget.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7-Byfob2kx" border="lg solid" border-sides="top" colspan="20"><display size="md" class="metric">$2.61M</display><p font-size="sm" class="gloss">Forecast at completion, an assumption that is $210K and 8.75% over.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="hug" class="columns"><grid-item id="BJRbXraNKX" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>The driver</h4><p font-size="sm">Tessera Tax was added in April 2026 after Nomad missed 11 jurisdictions. Build cost is $164K; a $48K annual licence upsize remains unsigned.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3sShyyhKd1" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>What you need to do</h4><p font-size="sm">$60K contingency remains. The forecast assumes planned effort for the remaining waves and the current Phase 3 design; neither is tested. A revised paper reached the CFO on 11 September. Chase it in week one.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="f3TJk9wVqz"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Wxf5SIuW8k"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">02 · Where things stand</p><h1>Invoice accuracy improved fourfold but has stalled short of target</h1><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="mUmdtX8puD" class="evidence" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><graph chart-type="column" show-data-labels="true" y-axis-min="0" goal-value="0.5" goal-label="December target" width="490pt" height="250pt"><properties><property key="month" label="Month" type="label"></property><property key="rate" label="Invoices requiring correction (%)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>June 2026</cell><cell>4.8</cell></row><row><cell>September 2026</cell><cell>1.3</cell></row></data></graph><p role="caption" class="gloss"><b>Figure 2 —</b> Manual correction rate against the 0.5% December target, which remains an unvalidated planning assumption.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wdbpi4bqfB" class="prose" colspan="23"><h3>31 open tickets</h3><p><b>19</b> EU tax rounding, 61% of the total.</p><p><b>7</b> mid-cycle proration, 23%.</p><p><b>5</b> currency-conversion timing, 16%.</p><hr class="rule"><p>The last three weeks show no improvement. The proration adapter needs rework, and that work is not scheduled.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The 19 EU rounding tickets are the same items reported under tax integration and in the risk register. One count, three places.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="PRXOxyjE7j" vertical-align="center" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none" class="act"><grid-item id="NKc-Pv-13i" background-color="palette-2"><display size="xl" class="metric"><span text-color="palette-3">03</span></display><hr color="palette-3" thickness="md" width="xxs" class="tick"><h1>How it runs</h1><p font-size="lg">The meetings that control the work, the systems you need, the incident path and the commercial terms that matter with Nomad.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="7eGhPEJC2k"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Zw0GWhSDx4"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">03 · How it runs</p><h1>The operating cadence</h1><table col-widths="[25,18,57]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="ledger"><tbody><tr><td><p>When</p></td><td><p>Forum</p></td><td><p>What matters</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Monday 09:30 · 15 min</p></td><td><p><b>Squad standup</b></p></td><td><p>Whole delivery team. Blockers only.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Wednesday 14:00 · 45 min</p></td><td><p><b>Wave review</b></p></td><td><p>Go or no-go and exception triage. Hannah chairs; you approve. The review before a wave Thursday is decisive.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Alternate Thursday 16:00 · 30 min</p></td><td><p><b>Steering</b></p></td><td><p>CFO, CTO and VP RevOps. Present status, budget and decisions. Pack due Wednesday noon.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>First three business days monthly</p></td><td><p><b>Close check-in</b></p></td><td><p>With the Controller. Non-negotiable because billing blocks the close.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Quarterly</p></td><td><p><b>Vendor review</b></p></td><td><p>With Nomad’s CSM. Next meeting: 14 October.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><hr class="rule"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" class="claim"><grid-item id="akIEb-UHwI" colspan="14"><labels><label variant="plain" text-color="accent">RULE</label></labels></grid-item><grid-item id="WLDfbnvx4E" colspan="46"><p>Cancel the standup before you cancel the wave review.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="DfYFBvdVU_"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Ueoq6jz-Y9"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">03 · How it runs</p><h1>Where everything lives</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" vertical-sizing="fill" class="columns"><grid-item id="xGD1Itzx6b" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>Runbooks and design</h4><p font-size="sm">Confluence space <b>BILL</b>, index page “Meridian Home”.</p><h4>Work tracking</h4><p font-size="sm">Jira project <b>MER</b>. Migration waves are epics MER-400 to MER-415.</p><h4>Production access</h4><p font-size="sm">IAM group <b>billing-admin</b>. Request through Access Portal; CTO approval; 24-hour turnaround.</p><h4>Sandbox</h4><p font-size="sm"><b>nomad-sbx-2</b>, refreshed from production every Sunday.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ctsnXwnMk2" class="prose" colspan="30"><h4>Dashboards</h4><p font-size="sm">Looker folder <b>“Meridian Ops”</b>: wave burndown, exception rate and cash collected.</p><h4>Incidents</h4><p font-size="sm">Slack <b>#meridian-oncall</b> and PagerDuty service <b>“Billing Platform”</b>.</p><h4>Commercial files</h4><p font-size="sm">Drive folder <b>“Meridian / Commercial”</b>. It holds contracts and the funding paper and is restricted to the steering group.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="oWzXAseRdg"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="87ijcCD47l"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">03 · How it runs</p><h1>What to do when billing breaks</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" marker="number" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="steps"><grid-item id="e8QGwNF4C7" vertical-align="center" padding="12pt 0"><p><b>Declare in #meridian-oncall and page Billing Platform.</b> The on-call engineer leads the incident; you handle communications.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="9nRKUl_kn7" vertical-align="center" padding="12pt 0"><p><b>Check the latest wave first.</b> Most incidents have followed a wave within 72 hours. The rollback script is at BILL/runbooks/wave-rollback.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="tkYkLyyL2V" vertical-align="center" padding="12pt 0"><p><b>Never edit invoices directly in Nomad.</b> Use a credit note and reissue or the audit trail breaks revenue recognition.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="APkmdGAD5W" vertical-align="center" padding="12pt 0"><p><b>Open a P1 vendor ticket within 30 minutes.</b> Nomad’s SLA clock starts with the ticket, not the phone call.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="prHMCGRD3D" vertical-align="center" padding="12pt 0"><p><b>Tell Finance before customers.</b> The Controller decides whether an invoice run is held.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="vEKc--RTMc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="-lFf-pOwIe"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">03 · How it runs</p><h1>The vendor relationship, in the terms that matter</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="sidehead"><grid-item id="JzFskK5fx3" padding="11pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="yG3NY8YGHu" colspan="14"><h4>People</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="eOjk0UpyXj" colspan="40"><p>Nomad Billing. CSM Elena Petrova holds weekly office hours on Thursdays.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="77Rtkk-1R6" padding="11pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="bFeQ9ZWZh-" colspan="14"><h4>Contract</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="Gjdw4sajoo" colspan="40"><p>$310K a year, three-year term to 31 March 2029. Renewal notice is 90 days; diary 31 December 2028.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="Pc6nPdbYXQ" padding="11pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="pgxCtCpkp7" colspan="14"><h4>Support</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="NaAfvvkYSr" colspan="40"><p>P1 response in two hours; P2 in one business day. Credits must be claimed within 30 days. Kestrel has never claimed one.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="gXI99p9xq-" padding="11pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="7ml2EXVXtn" colspan="14"><h4>Roadmap</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="PUphypkeb6" colspan="40"><p>Multi-currency payouts are committed for Q1 2027. Native EU tax expansion is unscheduled.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="z_WsT5wQLE" padding="11pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="CwSWOPk_K4" colspan="14"><h4>Working style</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="rnNCueDa7E" colspan="40"><p>The relationship is good but transactional. Elena responds to written escalation, not Slack.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VNzwv2IDHW" vertical-align="center" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none" class="act"><grid-item id="gQhZKIlutB" background-color="palette-2"><display size="xl" class="metric"><span text-color="palette-3">04</span></display><hr color="palette-3" thickness="md" width="xxs" class="tick"><h1>People and decisions</h1><p font-size="lg">Who owns the work, which calls are settled, which are waiting for you, and the risks and dependencies that do not fit a tidy status line.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="HUvEk-33uM"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="unay1nsyj6"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">04 · People and decisions</p><h1>Who owns what</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" marker="icon" marker-position="inline" marker-align="start" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="10pt 14pt" class="roles"><grid-item id="qcY5YpTkjX" colspan="60"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/b3ixZPPHhbrZgkjxED3BoK.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="executive finance sponsor approval"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>Dana Whitfield, CFO</b><br>Sponsor. Owns funding, scope changes and the year-end call. Decides; does not attend detail.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="bX5IBqMCgq" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/rvG8r7JW3pVBhQhojffR.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="project owner delivery steering"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>You, project owner</b><br>Own delivery, budget, the steering pack and every open decision in this section.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cZ6YdhHxFL" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/RU15TlyKVXLmq40YxKpL.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="software engineering lead architecture"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>Marcus Oyelaran, Engineering Lead</b><br>Platform build, proration adapter and complex-account patterns. Sole expert on the adapter.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XjkzzhXLEH" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/rtayXmC23ZkFAh5kKFq9.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="revenue operations migration planning"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>Hannah Blum, RevOps Manager</b><br>Wave planning, customer communications and the go or no-go recommendation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="TkC4D1ZU4q" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/8dbmXY263dMFbs87Fmkac3.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="finance systems tax ledger"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>Tomás Iriarte, Finance Systems Lead</b><br>Tax, revenue recognition and close readiness.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="z6HpQpGAyt" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/ALwwg82HS65rdGuUK77Y.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="quality assurance test checklist"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>Wei Zhang, QA</b><br>Wave regression suite and exception triage.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZYO9-UjVrH" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/HgqDnphKdWwmqsXJsxla.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="data platform api dependency"></icon></grid-item-label><p><b>Sanjay Rao, Data Platform</b><br>Owns the metering API. He is a dependency, not a Meridian team member.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The team has eleven people. Five engineers report to Marcus, not to you.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="n2C2G3SogX"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Vu0Lj74kAD"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">04 · People and decisions</p><h1>Five decisions already made. Reopen these only with new evidence</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" marker="symbol" marker-size="large" marker-label="✓" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="checks"><grid-item id="Fe3ufywHWD" padding="10pt 0"><p><b>Buy, not build. February 2026.</b> Build was costed at 26 engineer-months against an 18-month deadline.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="_73tP2w7QX" padding="10pt 0"><p><b>Waves, not big bang. March 2026.</b> Finance would not accept one cutover across a close period.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nTPyigDbTX" padding="10pt 0"><p><b>Tessera Tax over Nomad native tax. April 2026.</b> Nomad covered 23 of 34 jurisdictions. It caused the overrun; my judgment is that it was still the right call.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="NayH12MQE9" padding="10pt 0"><p><b>Keep BillingSvc read-only. May 2026.</b> Audit needs FY26 and FY27 history to remain queryable.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7yrUTKjOM1" padding="10pt 0"><p><b>Do not migrate the 40 perpetual-licence accounts. July 2026.</b> Migration cost exceeded remaining revenue. This is why the denominator is 1,140, not 1,180.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="9Fthf5Osvr"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="3krXNaHuLN"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">04 · People and decisions</p><h1>Four decisions are waiting for you</h1><table col-widths="[27,49,13,11]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="ledger"><tbody><tr><td><p>Decision</p></td><td><p>Why it matters</p></td><td><p>Due</p></td><td><p>Sponsor</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Revenue recognition before or after year-end close?</b></p></td><td><p>Before close puts Phase 2 completion and the close on Tomás in the same three weeks. After close means two months of manual schedules.</p></td><td><p>6 Nov</p></td><td><p>CFO</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Who owns dunning policy?</b></p></td><td><p>Finance and Customer Success each say the other team owns it. The answer blocks Phase 3 build.</p></td><td><p>16 Oct</p></td><td><p>You</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Sign the $48K Tessera upsize?</b></p></td><td><p>The current tier caps at 25,000 calculations a month; August reached 23,100.</p></td><td><p>30 Oct</p></td><td><p>CFO</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Set a BillingSvc decommission date.</b></p></td><td><p>The work is unfunded and unowned while hosting costs $7K a month. Put a date into steering.</p></td><td><p>At steering</p></td><td><p>CFO</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5NouxDitdq"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="v7fmCT_e-4"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">04 · People and decisions</p><h1>Risk register</h1><table col-widths="[28,14,43,15]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" class="ledger"><tbody><tr><td><p>Risk</p></td><td><p>Rating</p></td><td><p>Mitigation or decision</p></td><td><p>Owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Complex-account migration slips</b></p></td><td background-color="palette-1"><p>High, likely</p></td><td><p>88 accounts; no pattern; design due 23 October. Marcus is prototyping three archetypes. Fallback: extend waves into February.</p></td><td><p>Marcus</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Proration key-person dependency</b></p></td><td background-color="palette-1"><p>High</p></td><td><p>Marcus alone understands the adapter. Pairing sessions were cancelled twice. Still unresolved.</p></td><td><p>You</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Wave 15 on 31 December</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p>Holiday cover is thin and Finance is closed. Moving it shifts the final wave to 28 January. Decide on 16 December.</p></td><td><p>Hannah</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>EU tax rounding</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p>19 open tickets with small customer-visible amounts.</p></td><td><p>Tomás</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Budget approval refused or trimmed</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p>Would stop the Tessera upsize and cap throughput.</p></td><td><p>You</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>January close contention</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p>Finance capacity is fully committed in weeks 1 to 3.</p></td><td><p>Tomás</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Vendor slips multi-currency payouts</b></p></td><td><p>Low, contractual</p></td><td><p>Q1 2027 commitment; APAC expansion depends on it.</p></td><td><p>You</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="wx_iJ9oE_P"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="bDkhnOLb5a"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">04 · People and decisions</p><h1>Four things you depend on and do not control</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="S45FNInDG-" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/cdT645liJFWvFDXm6hPT.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="data api pipeline dependency" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A series of connected rectangles of varying sizes, forming a linear sequence, embodying the concept of a pipeline.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Metering API v3</h3><p font-size="sm">Data Platform, due 20 November. Phase 3 usage billing cannot be tested without it. Sanjay Rao has flagged a two-week risk. Check weekly.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="lT6-fZJXJJ" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/TntEzmEMZwRCgPTLV0Q7.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="salesforce field mapping lock" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black field or empty space enclosed by a white boundary, symbolizing a void, area, or region.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>CPQ field-mapping freeze</h3><p font-size="sm">Deal Desk. Kira Lund agreed no schema changes until 31 January, covering the last wave. The agreement is unwritten; get it in email.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FVvI-be36Y" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/tEhG5bzA7oXaXW8nvk6S.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="procurement contract approval" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black shopping cart or shopping bag shape within a white circle, conveying the concept of procurement or purchasing goods and services.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Tessera commercial approval</h3><p font-size="sm">Procurement needs two weeks once the CFO decision lands.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="t5qLxAvrbN" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/dFZm6AgW3p3IIHjlnhhu.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="pricing experiment checkout" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A beaker with a curved bottom and a narrow neck, often associated with scientific testing and trial.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Growth pricing experiment</h3><p font-size="sm">Runs to 30 November. Checkout redesign waits for its result; do not let Growth start earlier.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The PCI scope-change security review closed on 12 August. That dependency is done.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="HN9K8_sEGs"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="BavArJGJM8"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">04 · People and decisions</p><h1>Open questions nobody has answered</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="faq"><grid-item id="Ww6HXH2nK2" padding="10pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="2YBa7wTtk6" colspan="18"><h4>Who owns billing after Meridian?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="6us42AekdL" colspan="36"><p font-size="sm">There is no permanent operating team. Resolve this before Phase 3, not after.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="HtDQQs4Mrq" padding="10pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="FMhAjwlNQk" colspan="18"><h4>What is the real accuracy target?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="dZkv1Pmrhy" colspan="36"><p font-size="sm">The 0.5% target came from a workshop and was never validated against customer tolerance. Treat it as an assumption.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="uNF974qpnQ" padding="10pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="tNbTxgJ5oP" colspan="18"><h4>Will the 41 bespoke arrangements be standardised?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="0MIqhXo4t2" colspan="36"><p font-size="sm">Sales has resisted twice. Migrating them as-is embeds them for years.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="kNayDxv6TV" padding="10pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="vUb8i6fttA" colspan="18"><h4>Is the three-year payback credible?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="zTWfav_4Tn" colspan="36"><p font-size="sm">The original assumption excluded a tax engine and expected FY27 decommission. Neither condition now holds.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="aU4C7z0lYD" padding="10pt 0"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="dCnqo99aYo" colspan="18"><h4>Should the 40 perpetual accounts run off untouched?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="02trCUdELS" colspan="36"><p font-size="sm">The July 2026 carve-out has not been rechecked against BillingSvc’s $7K monthly hosting cost.</p></grid-item><spacer span="6"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="7BluZSy4Q4"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="9FKpBGZkPC"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">05 · Your first ninety days</p><h1>Your first ninety days</h1><p font-size="lg" class="lede">Day one is 1 October. The three blocks end on 30 October, 29 November and 29 December.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="fill" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="t3OHnpmbfZ" colspan="20"><h3>Days 1–30</h3><p font-size="sm">Chase funding. Observe the 8 and 22 October waves without changing them. Sit in on the 14 October vendor review while I chair. Read the proration design with Marcus and reinstate pairing. Resolve dunning ownership by 16 October. Sign or refuse the Tessera upsize by 30 October.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="QH6VDmop8z" colspan="20"><h3>Days 31–60</h3><p font-size="sm">Take the complex-account design to steering with dates. Decide revenue-recognition timing by 6 November. Put the CPQ freeze in writing. Check Metering API v3 with Sanjay before 20 November. Name the owner of billing operations after Meridian.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3_2XpDXd4I" colspan="20"><h3>Days 61–90</h3><p font-size="sm">Settle the 31 December wave at the 16 December review. Reforecast with Phase 3 properly scoped. Set the decommission date. Validate or change the accuracy target. Book the January vendor review and chair it yourself.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="v7tNJ31Nno"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="E7_0pzMJub"><p role="eyebrow" class="meta">05 · Your first ninety days</p><h1>Week one, and how to reach me</h1><grid divider="0.75pt" marker="number" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" class="steps"><grid-item id="jAXlft-f4c" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Request billing-admin access on day one.</b> It takes 24 hours and blocks everything else.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1YRz3HmQpd" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Read BILL/Meridian Home end to end.</b> Allow roughly two hours; it is current to 19 September.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RBBbBm4OT4" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Meet Marcus, Hannah and Tomás individually</b> before your first steering meeting.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="poTAt762ql" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Sit in on the 7 October wave review</b>, the day before wave 9 ships, and say nothing.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="AJfAKJtava" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Chase the funding paper through the CFO’s EA</b>, not through the CFO.</p></grid-item></grid><hr class="rule"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" class="claim"><grid-item id="DATS8flG9z" colspan="14"><labels><label variant="plain" text-color="accent">HANDOVER</label></labels></grid-item><grid-item id="3skjGU0awe" colspan="46"><p>I shadow you until 9 October and answer questions until 30 October. After that I move to Data Platform; escalate to Marcus, then the CTO.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>